\title{My Notes on Productivity}
\p{Due to the unstructured nature of PhD life / knowledge work in general, I have been trying to come up with the most effective system to ensure I am [\em{Getting Things Done}](allenGettingThingsDone2015) (ironically I found this system actually not that helpful).}

\p{Since [Cal Newport](calnewport) is a professor (can relate to the knowledge work problem), I have been reading a lot of his stuff on productivity. I read [Deep Work](newportDeepWorkRules2016) awhile back and the guiding principles make sense to me. However, I still struggle to actually implement it.}
\p{I often refer back to [Atomic Habits](clearAtomicHabitsEasy2019) as it intuitively just makes so much sense to me.}
\ul{
  \li{\em{Start small}: starting a habit should take less than 2 minutes.}
  \li{\em{Never miss a habit twice}.}
  \li{\em{Habit anchors}: I am always going to run so now after I run I stretch, which has resulted in remarkable stretching consistency (see my [Weeknotes](007S)).}
  \li{\em{Habit tracking:} Something I am also implementing in my [[007S]] with [habitify](habitify.me).}
}

